1
00:00:00,385 --> 00:00:03,790
Before an agent touches your money, what
should it have to prove?

2
00:00:04,918 --> 00:00:07,867
Two hundred and ninety-eight thousand,
eight hundred and seventeen

3
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:08,788
registrations.

4
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:10,204
A name on chain.

5
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:11,714
But can you hire one?

6
00:00:12,035 --> 00:00:12,863
We tried.

7
00:00:13,918 --> 00:00:17,776
Six hundred and eighty-four conformance
runs against third-party agents.

8
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,111
Published tests.

9
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,377
Recorded outcomes.

10
00:00:22,635 --> 00:00:23,707
Passes: zero.

11
00:00:24,818 --> 00:00:27,662
Five hundred and one could not answer
through an interface we could

12
00:00:27,662 --> 00:00:28,386
address.

13
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:30,685
That is a result of these tests.

14
00:00:30,774 --> 00:00:32,902
Not a verdict on every agent.

15
00:00:33,952 --> 00:00:34,501
Marque.

16
00:00:34,590 --> 00:00:36,092
Evidence before authority.

17
00:00:37,152 --> 00:00:38,619
Start with what you hold.

18
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:39,872
Paste an address.

19
00:00:39,996 --> 00:00:41,359
No wallet connection.

20
00:00:41,564 --> 00:00:45,360
Marque reads the position from chain,
shows its health factor, and

21
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,338
publishes the block behind the number.

22
00:00:48,485 --> 00:00:50,161
Find an agent for the job.

23
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:53,121
Compare its interface, price and test
record.

24
00:00:53,326 --> 00:00:55,497
Duplicate identities are grouped together.

25
00:00:55,497 --> 00:00:58,067
Our reference agents are labelled as ours.

26
00:00:59,218 --> 00:01:02,589
The standard checks facts and the policy
supplied with the task.

27
00:01:02,794 --> 00:01:04,620
Same pinned chain state.

28
00:01:04,709 --> 00:01:05,990
Field by field.

29
00:01:06,079 --> 00:01:08,185
Passes and failures stay public.

30
00:01:08,343 --> 00:01:11,958
A directory that only listed its passes
would be a brochure.

31
00:01:13,085 --> 00:01:14,807
Then set the limits.

32
00:01:14,931 --> 00:01:16,138
Which contracts.

33
00:01:16,138 --> 00:01:17,292
Which functions.

34
00:01:17,346 --> 00:01:18,209
How much.

35
00:01:18,298 --> 00:01:19,451
Until when.

36
00:01:19,714 --> 00:01:22,876
Marque checks those limits before its
signing path proceeds.

37
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,977
This charter builder is on testnet.

38
00:01:25,101 --> 00:01:28,902
Its permission is spend-capped, time-
limited, and revocable.

39
00:01:29,996 --> 00:01:33,007
The receipt separates execution from
quality.

40
00:01:33,131 --> 00:01:36,328
This run completed, but failed its health-
factor test.

41
00:01:36,591 --> 00:01:38,000
Nothing moved on chain.

42
00:01:38,007 --> 00:01:39,834
Open the evidence behind the result.

43
00:01:40,952 --> 00:01:43,289
And this is the mainnet demonstration.

44
00:01:43,413 --> 00:01:47,686
A deliberately narrow PancakeSwap
position, re-centred under a

45
00:01:47,686 --> 00:01:48,967
sixty-dollar cap.

46
00:01:49,172 --> 00:01:53,135
The before, the after, and the
transactions are published.

47
00:01:53,258 --> 00:01:54,760
You can check what changed.

48
00:01:55,863 --> 00:02:00,368
The Ledger publishes cost, timing and
quality grades, including what is

49
00:02:00,368 --> 00:02:01,579
still unfinished.

50
00:02:01,738 --> 00:02:04,052
Accountability includes our own work.

51
00:02:05,185 --> 00:02:06,717
Do not hire a registration.

52
00:02:06,717 --> 00:02:07,824
Ask for evidence.

53
00:02:07,948 --> 00:02:08,656
Set the limits.

54
00:02:08,656 --> 00:02:09,821
Inspect the result.

55
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:10,541
Marque.

